From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Atharva Tyagi <tyagiatharva11@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 14:52:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ioLPDMmode: lean 16-bit output for offline Lagrangian
 dispersion

A 30-min sampling window at 5 s cadence is 451 dumps. At 186x186x122 that is 77 GB of
full fp32 output per window, of which a backward LPDM reads five 3-D fields and four 2-D
ones. Accumulating that across a wind-direction corpus is the binding storage constraint,
and upstream exposes no way to select output fields or reduce their precision -- the only
five IO parameters are ioOutputMode, inFile, outFileBase, frqOutput and towerIOSelector,
and binary mode walks the same variable list as netCDF.

Adds ONE optional parameter, ioLPDMmode, defaulting to 0 = upstream behaviour, so the
diff is inert unless asked for. With ioLPDMmode = 1:

  - only u, v, w, theta, TKE_0, fricVel, z0m, invOblen and the coordinate geometry are
    written; everything else is skipped
  - the five 3-D prognostic fields are stored as CF-packed 16-bit integers, with
    scale_factor and add_offset computed from each field's range in each file. CF packing
    rather than IEEE half: it is self-describing, every CF-aware reader unpacks it with no
    code change, and a uniform absolute resolution suits a velocity field that crosses
    zero better than a floating-point one does
  - xPos/yPos/zPos/topoPos/lat/lon go into the FIRST file a run produces and are omitted
    thereafter. They are rewritten byte-identically every dump, and at this grid they cost
    more than the packed prognostic fields they accompany

77 GB per window becomes about 19 GB.

Packing resolution is range/65534, uniform. For w over a typical window that is ~1e-4 m/s
against sigma_w ~ 0.36 m/s -- four orders of magnitude below the Monte-Carlo noise of the
dispersion estimator that consumes it, which is the standard the precision has to meet.
65534 rather than 65536 so both endpoints are representable and -32768 stays free.

THE RESULTING FILES ARE NOT RESTARTABLE, by construction: rho and pressure are absent.
Restart from a full dump written with ioLPDMmode = 0. The parameter help says so.
---
 SRC/IO/io.c        |  5 +++
 SRC/IO/io.h        |  5 +++
 SRC/IO/io_netcdf.c | 95 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 103 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

